          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000014\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The basket rescue is easy to follow and ends with the rabbit warm, though the repeated steps and Lily’s hunger leave the close somewhat flat.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000028\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The basket rescue is easy to follow and ends with the rabbit warm, though the repeated steps and Lily’s hunger leave the close somewhat flat.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000058\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Sam shares his bread to draw the rabbit into the basket, and the rescue ends concretely with it resting in a blanket; the prose is repetitive.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000023\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The kitten is coaxed into the basket and brought safely inside; the sequence is clear but told in repetitive, plain sentences.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000036\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The kitten is coaxed into the basket and brought safely inside; the sequence is clear but told in repetitive, plain sentences.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000017\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Ben gives up his bread to help the stranded puppy, with a clear rescue and warm final image; the narration is repetitive.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000053\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Sam shares bread to coax the rabbit into a lowered basket, and it ends safely indoors; the prose is functional but repetitive.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000021\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The puppy’s fear is addressed by offering bread before the basket rescue, but the simple, repetitive narration offers little buildup.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Nora steadies a ladder while Dad lifts the kitten down, ending with the kitten warm; the rescue works, though the bread motive is dropped.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000048\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Nora’s bread helps coax the rabbit into the basket, leading to a safe, warm ending; the sentences are clear but repetitive.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000002\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Lily steadies the ladder as Dad rescues the puppy, with a concrete warm ending, though her initial wish to eat bread is not developed.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000057\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Lily shares bread to get the rabbit into the lowered basket, completing a clear rescue; repeated actions make the prose plain.\",\"group_id\":0}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":2,\"causal_path\":2,\"ending\":2,\"language\":2,\"overall\":2},\"diversity_evidence\":\"Most stories use the same hungry child, shivering animal on a ledge, bread-and-basket rescue, and warm-blanket ending. The ladder rescue in s000034 and s000002 is a small causal variation; the other differences are chiefly names and animal substitutions. These sampled stories alone do not establish diversity of the entire generator.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"A child shares bread to coax a shivering animal from a high ledge into a lowered basket; the animal is brought indoors and warmed in a blanket.\"},{\"group_id\":1,\"summary\":\"A child steadies a ladder while an adult climbs up and lifts a shivering animal from a high ledge, then the child warms it indoors.\"}]}",
